{"name":"Starship","hex":"#e3dd39","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"starship","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of spacecraft capable of traveling to the solar systems of other stars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starship"}],"entries":[{"title":"Starship","blocks":[{"text":"A starship, starcraft, or interstellar spacecraft is a theoretical spacecraft designed for traveling between planetary systems. The term is mostly found in science fiction. Reference to a \"star-ship\" are found as early as 1882 in Oahspe: A New Bible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Modern_Pulsed_Fission_Propulsion_Concept.jpg/330px-Modern_Pulsed_Fission_Propulsion_Concept.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starship"},{"title":"Starship (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Starship is an American rock band from San Francisco, California. Initially a continuation of Jefferson Starship, it underwent a change in musical direction, the subsequent loss of personnel, and a lawsuit settlement that led to a name change. Starship's 1985 album, Knee Deep in the Hoopla, was certified platinum by the RIAA, and included two singles that went to number one on the US Billboard Hot 100 chart: \"We Built This City\" and \"Sara\". Their follow up album, No Protection, released in 1987, was certified gold and featured the band's third number one single, \"Nothing's Gonna Stop Us Now\". After a short hiatus in the early 1990s, the band reformed in 1992 as \"Starship featuring Mickey Thomas\" and resumed touring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Starship2010.jpg/330px-Starship2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starship_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Daedalus_Spaceship_concept.jpg/500px-Daedalus_Spaceship_concept.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Daedalus_Spaceship_concept.jpg/500px-Daedalus_Spaceship_concept.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's conception of British Interplanetary Society's Project Daedalus (1978), a fusion powered interstellar probe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaedalus_Spaceship_concept.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Stanford_Torus-based_generation_ship.png/500px-Stanford_Torus-based_generation_ship.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Stanford_Torus-based_generation_ship.png/500px-Stanford_Torus-based_generation_ship.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stanford Torus-based generation ship, proposed by Project Hyperion[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStanford_Torus-based_generation_ship.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wormhole_travel_as_envisioned_by_Les_Bossinas_for_NASA.jpg/500px-Wormhole_travel_as_envisioned_by_Les_Bossinas_for_NASA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wormhole_travel_as_envisioned_by_Les_Bossinas_for_NASA.jpg/500px-Wormhole_travel_as_envisioned_by_Les_Bossinas_for_NASA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's depiction of a hypothetical Wormhole Induction Propelled Spacecraft, based loosely on the 1994 \"warp drive\" paper of Miguel Alcubierre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWormhole_travel_as_envisioned_by_Les_Bossinas_for_NASA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/NCC-1701_Prop.